# Pull request base branch

- **Default base branch for PRs:** `development`
- **Never** open PRs against `main` unless the user explicitly requests a release/hotfix to `main`.
- When creating a branch for new work, branch from `development`.
- When using `gh pr create`, always pass `--base development`.
- `main` is the production/release branch; changes reach it via merge from `development` (or an explicit release PR).

```bash
# ✅ Correct
gh pr create --base development --head feature/my-change --title "..." --body "..."

# ❌ Wrong (unless explicitly requested)
gh pr create --base main ...
```
